Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485:

- A scene without `orthogonalprojection` (absent or null) is a 3D scene: the loader (GH 0x1401b6c60)
  flags a scene orthographic only for an object with a width and height. LWE required the member
  ("Projection must have a width"), so the three 3D scenes of the corpus didn't load (G24).
- The perspective (GH 0x1401b3f70): the effective fov (vertical, degrees, clamped 0.1–179.9 in the
  camera update GH 0x1401b8af0), the target's aspect, general nearz/farz. The view is a right-handed
  lookAt (GH 0x1401cb340) of the active camera object — the last visible one: eye = its world
  translation, centre = eye − its z axis, up = its y axis, its `fov` — else of camera.eye/center/up.
  The shake (GH 0x1401c7680) moves eye and centre by (cos t, sin 1.333t, sin t), length^roughness³,
  × amplitude · 0.1.
- An object's matrix (GH 0x1401b5170): parent world · T(origin) · R · S, R from the angles as
  Rz · Ry · Rx (GH 0x14020af40). In a 3D scene an image layer (not full-screen or passthrough) draws
  its quad in its own space (alignment anchored at the origin) through that matrix and the camera;
  full-screen layers keep the 2D layout over the target. Particles take the 3D camera in LWE's scene
  space. Only angles.z and a 2D origin were used before (G22).
- Model objects (`"model": "x.mdl"`, G25; the factory tries `model` first, GH 0x1401be650): the MDL
  meshes (B12's loader, now also reading normals and tangents, format bits 0x2 / 0x4), each drawn
  with the material it names (generic4) into the scene's target, which gets a depth buffer.
- Lights (G26, E13): lpoint/lspot objects (properties GH 0x140283df0) packed as WE's
  g_LCluster_Origin/Color/Direction/Extra (GH 0x1401bf270): (position, radius), (colour · intensity,
  exponent), (a spot's world x axis, 1 / (cos inner − cos outer)), (−cos outer / that). The
  generated PerformLighting_V1 (GH 0x140197e20) is now WE's point/spot loop over them with
  ComputePBRLightShadow; it returned 0.
- Fog (G28, E14): general fogdistance*/fogheight* (registered GH 0x1401c7880) fed as WE builds
  them (GH 0x1401ba300): params = (start, end − start, startdensity, enddensity − startdensity); a
  model material keeping generic4's FOG combo gets FOG_DIST / FOG_HEIGHT.
- A texture whose flags have bits LWE doesn't know (0x800000 on 3509243656's PBR masks) loads; it
  was rejected ("unknown texture flags").

Ours (not decoded): a 3D scene renders 1920x1080 (WE: the output's size); `transparentsorting` draws
each run of world-placed objects back to front by origin distance; a model material without
depthtest/depthwrite enables them; culling is off for models (the y flip of the target turns the
winding over); a point light's direction terms (0, 1); at most 8 lights, no clusters.

Not done: shadows (shadow atlas), light cookies, volumetrics, tube/directional lights, shape
(volume light) objects, skinned/morphed models, reflection, the 3D camera's parallax, zoom and
camera paths, image `perspective` layers in 2D scenes, perspectiveoverridefov, fog on image and
particle shaders, sortorder/customsortorder, hit-testing world-placed layers.

